d by G. Gleig, page 504:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(historical) An English gold coin, bearing the figure of the archangel Michael, circulated between the 15th and 17th centuries, and varying in value from six shillings and eightpence to ten shillings.", "tags": ["historical"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["angel-noble"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(military slang, originally Royal Air Force) An altitude, measured in thousands of feet.", "tags": ["slang"], "examples": ["Climb to angels sixty."], "quotes": [{"text": "And even now part of me flies over Dresden at angels one five; / Though they’ll never fathom it, behind my sarcasm desperate memories lie.", "reference": "1983 March 21, Roger Waters, “The Hero's Return”, in The Final Cut, performed by Pink Floyd:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(colloquial, dated) An unidentified flying object detected by air traffic control radar.", "tags": ["colloquial", "dated"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "someone that funds", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": [{"definition": "(finance) An angel investor.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "“Latent” angels are defined as those who have not invested capital in the past 12 months, although they likely have invested knowledge in the process of reviewing potential investments.", "reference": "2011, OECD, Financing High-Growth Firms: The Role of Angel Investors:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(theater) The person who funds a show.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["backer"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}], "synonyms": ["errand-ghost"],